Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||02-10-2001||07:59 PM||||Wife and I are driving the my white 86 GT and we leave a traffic light and I sort of blast up over a long bridge and leave everyone behind. However in the rear view mirror I notice an older Chevy Citation is moving up fast. Before I can get to the other side of the bridge I get passed by this car and its driven by a gray haired lady about 75 years of age. We can't believe it but she just flys down the road and leaves us behind.<P>I come up to the next red light and she's sittin in the left lane. Joking with my wife I say lets challenge her to a race. My wife says no way. The light changes but the lady hesitates a second. I just wait. Then she slowly starts off. I think she was baiting me. I keep pace with her as she accelerates then she punches it and either flipped me the bird or saluted in the rear view mirror, I'm not sure which. I let her go not wanting to be responsible for contributing to any accident which might have befallen her.<P>Dave<P>86 GT ||||reg||1
